{"authoredAt":"2026-08-20T12:52:41.099Z","conclusion":"findings","findings":[{"category":"adversarial","desc":"quality-cleanup: packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts:74 delegates releaseProviderProcessAdmission to the throwing releaseProviderProcessSlot primitive even though production callers invoke it from bare finally/catch cleanup paths (packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts:2484 and packages/main/src/core/planned-steps-executor.ts:470). An unlink or registry-lock failure therefore replaces the real provider exception or converts a successful provider run into a hard CLI error, contradicting the registry module’s explicit best-effort-finally contract at packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts:354. Route the adapter through releaseProviderProcessSlotBestEffort so release failure remains observable without hijacking provider control flow.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["packages/main/src/core/lattice-dispatch.ts","packages/main/src/core/planned-steps-executor.ts","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts"],"severity":"medium"}],"lane":"lattice-review-quality","providerAgent":"lattice-review-quality","readLog":{"digest":"db0aadfb6c7b4225a78df0b52d719a295c3616ffd5a66cd1e250fed273b68e18","filesReadFully":[".lattice/story/actives/B-137a/background.md",".lattice/story/actives/B-137a/plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts","packages/main/src/core/managed-review-evidence.ts","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-admission.ts","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts","packages/main/src/handlers/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/handlers/managed-review-evidence.ts"],"filesTriagedByName":[".lattice/story/actives/B-137a/candidate-spec-set.json",".lattice/story/actives/B-137a/checklist.json","docs/host-run-usage.md","docs/requirements/decisions/cli-engine-english-open-source-ex